  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "They had the go-ahead run in the seventh and watched it evaporate by the eighth.",
    "what_this_means": "The shape of this game says everything. Yankees scraped together ten hits, drove in runs when they needed them most, and still lost by six because one inning didn't hold. Garc\u00eda flipped a 6\u20135 deficit with a solo shot in the seventh. The kind of moment teams build on, except they didn't. The bullpen fractured. Chivilli gave up six runs in the eighth, and suddenly a one-run lead became a five-run deficit in minutes. This wasn't a collapse spread across nine innings. This was a collapse compressed into one. They had the moments. The finish never arrived. Wells drove in two, Garc\u00eda drove in two more, but the margin vanished when it mattered most. A one-run lead after seven innings is not a plan. It's a vulnerability waiting for exactly what happened.",
    "what_to_watch": "Hunter Dobbins takes the mound tonight with a 3.74 ERA. Ryan Weathers has thrown 2.93 over his last four starts and gets the ball to answer.",
